{"url": "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/requirements.cfm", "final_url": "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/requirements.cfm", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "Skip to main content\nShow\nMenu\nUNIVERSITY ANNOUNCEMENT\nNotice for AU employees: Learn More\nYou are here:\nAmerican University\nCollege of Arts & Sciences\nCAS Admissions\nRequirements and Deadlines\nGraduate Admissions Home\nDegrees & Programs\nHow to Apply\nEvents & Visits for Prospective Students\nRequirements & Deadlines\nInternational Applicants\nTuition, Funding & Scholarships\nPartnerships\nStaff\nFor Admitted Students\nCONTACT US\n202-885-3620\ncasgrad@american.edu\nMonday-Friday, 9:00-5:00; please allow 1 business day for responses.\nBattelle Tompkins, Room T-21\non a map\nCAS-Graduate Admissions\n4400 Massachusetts Avenue NW\nWashington, DC 20016-8081 United States\nRequirements and Deadlines\nReady to Apply?\nOnce you've found the graduate program that fits your goals, it's time to start your application! You\u2019ll complete the process through our online application system, where you\u2019ll be asked to submit a form along with a set of required documents and materials.\nTo help you stay on track, we\u2019ve put together lists of everything you\u2019ll need by program, along with important deadlines.\nInternational applicants: Please note that there are a few additional requirements for students applying from outside the United States. Be sure to review those carefully as you prepare your materials.\nApplication Materials\nAll programs require:\nStatement of Purpose\nTranscripts\nResume or CV\nInternational Students\nSome may require:\nStandardized Test Scores\nLetters of Recommendation\nPortfolio or Writing Sample\nPriority Deadlines\nPriority Deadlines are for first-round consideration for admission and graduate funding. Applications received by this time are guaranteed full review for the upcoming semester. Applications received after the deadline are reviewed in order of receipt provided there is still available space in the cohort. The admissions committee reserves the right to push late applications to the next available semester\u2019s review panels.\nTo be considered for a priority deadline, your online application form and fee must be received by the date listed. All supporting documents (statement of purpose, transcripts, recommendation letters, etc.) should be uploaded within five business days.\nInternational applicants requiring a VISA may have additional deadlines. Visit our International Applicants page for more details.\nRequirements & Deadlines by Program\nMaster's Degrees\nApplied Economics (MS, online)\nArt History (MA)\nArtificial Intelligence (MS)\nArts Management (MA)\nAudio Technology (MA)\nBiology (MS)\nComputer Science (MS)\nCreative Writing (MFA)\nData Science (MS)\nEconomics (MS)\nEnvironmental Science (MS)\nEthics, Peace & Human Rights (MA)\nGame Design (MA)\nHealth Promotion (MS)\nHistory (MA)\nInternational Economics (MA)\nLiterature, Culture & Technology (MA)\nNutrition Education (MS, online)\nPhilosophy (MA)\nPsychology (MA)\nPublic Anthropology (MA)\nPublic Health, Innovation & Practice (MA)\nPublic History (MA)\nSociology Research & Practice (MA)\nSpanish & Latin American Studies (MA)\nStatistics (MS)\nStudio Art (MFA)\nTeaching English to Speakers of Other Languages \u2014 TESOL (MA)\nPhD Programs\nAnthropology (PhD)\nBehavior, Cognition & Neuroscience (PhD)\nBiomedical & Environmental Health Sciences (PhD)\nClinical Psychology (PhD)\nComputational Science & AI (PhD)\nEconomics (PhD)\nHistory (PhD)\nCertificates\nApplied Microeconomics\nApplied Statistics\nArts Management\nAsian Studies\nAudio Production\nClinical Biochemistry\nData Science\nGender Analysis in Economics\nGlobal Health & Culture\nInternational Arts Management\nInternational Economic Relations\nNutrition Education (online)\nPost-Baccalaureate Premedical\nPublic Anthropology\nPublic Sociology\nSocial Res